        <h2 class="faqHome__title">
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </h2>
      

      <div class="faqHome__wrap"><div class="faqHome__item " bid="qa_39YHdB">
            <question>
              What is a DTF transfer?
            </question>
            <answer>DTF stands for Direct-to-Film, a printing method where your design is printed onto a special film and then heat pressed onto a garment. DTF transfers work on a wide range of fabrics—including cotton, polyester, blends, and more—and can be applied in about 12-15 seconds with a heat press.</answer>
          </div><div class="faqHome__item " bid="qa_BrRrWw">
            <question>
              What is the minimum I can order?
            </question>
            <answer>No Minimums! Whether you need 1 or 100,000 we can do it!</answer>
          </div><div class="faqHome__item " bid="qa_8ERyRm">
            <question>
              What kind of press do I need?
            </question>
            <answer>You can use the iron you have lying around your house or an industrial level heat press or anything in between. Learn more on our <a href="https://ninjatransfers.com/pages/application-instructions-for-dtf-transfers-heat-sources" title="Application Instructions for DTF Transfers | Heat Sources">How to Press</a> page.</answer>
          </div><div class="faqHome__item " bid="qa_w7ePqi">
            <question>
              What sizes are available?
            </question>
            <answer>We have sizes from 2" X 2" to 24" X 30 feet</answer>
          </div><div class="faqHome__item " bid="qa_iEwBxk">
            <question>
              How do transfers hold up in the wash?
            </question>
            <answer>Ninja Transfers have been rigorously tested and verified by third party to ensure long-lasting durability. After undergoing 100 machine wash cycles (80°F, normal cycle, line dry) on a 100% cotton shirt, the transfers were evaluated for color retention, peeling, cracking, and overall integrity. The results were overwhelmingly positive, with a "Satisfactory" grade across all criteria, including negligible hand-feel change and no significant signs of delamination or print detachment.</answer>
          </div><div class="faqHome__item " bid="qa_gtcGFy">
            <question>
              How quickly can I get my order?
            </question>
            <answer>Expedited orders ship within 24 -48 hours.</answer>
          </div><div class="faqHome__item " bid="qa_qEe7yD">
            <question>
              What file format should my artwork be?
            </question>
            <answer>Vector art is always preferred, raster art should be at least 300 dpi. Preferred file types: .AI, .PDF Accepted files types: .JPG, .PNG</answer>
          </div><div class="faqHome__item " bid="qa_6BdMzf">
            <question>
              What is your refund policy?
            </question>
            <answer>We stand behind our work so If you have any issues with your transfers at all <a href="https://ninjatransfers.com/pages/contact" title="Contact Us | Ninja Transfers">Contact Us </a>and we'll be sure to make sure we solve whatever issue you might have.</answer>
          </div></div>
